Blocked: a multi-line body may not be passed inline with --body/-b.

  command: gh pr edit -R foo/bar --title a\ b --body $'line1\nline2'

Combining --body "$(...)" with a heredoc stacks two layers of quoting, and a
mis-escape — a stray backslash before a backtick — ends up in the published
text.

Fix: write the body to a file (a scratchpad, say) and pass --body-file
instead of --body:
  gh pr edit -R owner/repo ... --body-file /path/to/body.md
